{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607071610-kotoba-lang-kisekae-vrm-character-editor"
  :title "ADR-2607071610: kotoba-lang/kisekae -- VRM character editor as a domain library
          (spec-as-artifact, org-vrmc-vrm engine, kotobase persistence)"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang-kisekae"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-07"
  :authoritative_for
  ["the VRM character editor lives at kotoba-lang/kisekae as a pure-.cljc DOMAIN library
    (no UI) over org-vrmc-vrm's existing decompose/compose/export engine -- the editor
    layer was the missing piece, not the engine"
   "the character spec (small plain EDN: base URL, part overrides, material edits, user
    meta) is the artifact of record; the .vrm is deterministically rebuilt from it on
    demand, never stored as the truth"
   "dress-up semantics: one override per part kind (replace, not stack); :body is never
    overridable (the base's skeleton is compose's :skeleton-base); part vocabulary
    derives from vrm.part/part-categories, never a parallel list"
   "edits are data ({:op/type ...}), applied by one pure fn; unknown ops / unfetched URLs
    / missing donor parts THROW -- never silent no-ops or substitutions"
   "persistence is a SpecStore protocol with MemSpecStore built+tested now, plus the pure
    kotobase datom mapping (spec->tx/entity->spec, document-as-datom); the kotobase-backed
    record via the :db-api map is follow-up wiring, not design"
   "runtime priority honestly applied: interop-free .cljc, cljs-executable today,
    kototama-subset by construction, zero #?(:kototama) branches (the feature doesn't
    exist); .kotoba numeric cores are recorded aspiration only"
   "UI belongs to consumers: canvaskit viewport + kami-webgpu preview + kotoba-lang/editor
    controls; first app is babiniku.net's create-your-character flow (ADR-2607071600 M6)"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607071600-net-babiniku-service-completion-design.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607071130-kotoba-lang-canvaskit-scroll-view-consolidation.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607021330 (kotoba-lang org visibility = public)"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "user direction 2026-07-07: 'vrm character editor なども kotoba-lang として、
           ユーザーが使いやすいものを再設計して. kotoba wasm, cljc, kotobase datomic' --
           confirmed 'do it'"
  :engine_already_exists
  {:what "kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm (restored from the deleted kami-vrm Rust crate,
          ADR-2607010930): vrm.part/decompose (parts classified #{:body :hair :face
          :outfit :accessory :other}, production-hardened name heuristic),
          vrm.compose/compose (cross-document merge onto a unified :skeleton-base),
          vrm.export/export-glb (VRM 1.0 GLB out, via kotoba-lang/glb), plus mtoon/
          expressions/springs/humanoid and zero-dep JSON+math"
   :missing "everything AROUND the engine: persisted document model of user choices,
             pure edit ops + undo/redo, selection logic into compose inputs, storage
             contract"}
  :adjacent_blocks "canvaskit (viewport gestures), editor (walk-EDN controls), webgpu
                    (preview), kotobase :db-api (persistence) -- compose, don't rebuild"}

 :decision
 {:library "kotoba-lang/kisekae (着せ替え) -- pure .cljc, one dep (org-vrmc-vrm), no UI;
            public repo, pushed @ adc47d0, 33-check bb gate, clj-kondo clean"
  :namespaces
  {:kisekae.spec "character-spec EDN + problem-list validation + overridable-kinds
                  derived from vrm.part/part-categories (minus :body :other) +
                  part-urls fetch-list"
   :kisekae.edit "ops (:op/rename :op/set-meta :op/add-part[replace-per-kind]
                  :op/remove-part :op/set-base-color), op-log history with undo/redo and
                  redo-tail truncation; unknown op throws"
   :kisekae.build "effective-sources (base minus overridden kinds + donor parts,
                   :skeleton-base tracked) -> compose -> apply-material-edits
                   (baseColorFactor) -> apply-meta (USER's name/authors/license) ->
                   export-glb; pure given docs-by-url, caller does I/O; missing anything
                   throws"
   :kisekae.store "SpecStore protocol + MemSpecStore (tested), spec->tx/entity->spec pure
                   datom mapping ({:kisekae/id :kisekae/name :kisekae/spec-edn},
                   document-as-datom) for the future kotobase-backed record via the
                   :db-api map"}
  :invariants
  ["spec is the artifact; .vrm is derived cache"
   ":body never overridable -- skeleton swapping is a rigging problem this editor does
     not pretend to solve"
   "fail loudly: no silent op drops, no silent part substitution"
   "license meta is first-class at export; base/donor license compatibility is the
    consuming app's concern to surface, not build's to fake-check"]
  :runtime_priority "interop-free .cljc; cljs today; kototama-subset by construction; no
                     #?(:kototama); .kotoba aspiration recorded, not claimed"}

 :consequences
 {:shipped "repo scaffolded/pushed/registered (west.yml, this landing commit); 33 checks"
  :followups ["compose->export integration test against a real fixture .vrm (synthetic
               docs cover selection/transforms; buffer merge rides the engine's own
               116-assertion suite meanwhile)"
              "kotobase-backed SpecStore (:db-api wiring)"
              "the editor app inside babiniku (ADR-2607071600 M6)"
              "expression/texture/spring-bone ops -- engine supports them; additive"]
  :first_consumer "net-babiniku gains the kisekae dependency at ADR-2607071600 M6"
  :addendum_2607071700
  {:context "building net-babiniku's actual cross-avatar part-swap UI (M6 slice 2)
             surfaced two real org-vrmc-vrm/vrm.compose bugs, invisible in every prior
             compose test/usage because those all composed parts from the SAME source
             document"
   :bug_1_fixed
   {:what "compose's skin rebuild grew a skin's :joints with donor joints but reused
           the base's own (shorter) inverseBindMatrices accessor unchanged -- real
           avatars threw 'No item N in vector of length N' loading the composed GLB"
    :fix "kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#1 (pin advanced): build a genuinely new IBM
          accessor spanning the grown joint list when growth occurs; regression test
          on a synthetic fixture confirmed to fail pre-fix with the same exception"}
   :bug_2_open
   {:what "compose's mesh/attribute remap only redirects which ACCESSOR a :JOINTS_0
           attribute points to, never remaps the per-vertex joint-index VALUES inside
           it -- those stay 'position in the donor's OWN original skin joint array',
           wrong once every mesh binds to the ONE unified skin's different joint order.
           Symptom: composed avatar loads (bug 1 fixed) but renders visibly distorted"
    :real_fix_scope "reorder compose's phases (joint-set/node-remap must resolve
                     BEFORE mesh merge, not after) + component-type-aware
                     decode/remap/re-encode of every donor mesh's JOINTS_0 data --
                     materially larger and riskier than bug 1, correctly deferred
                     rather than attempted blind in the cycle that found it"
    :blocks "net-babiniku M6 slice 2 (cross-avatar part-swap); M6 slice 1 (reuse base
             avatar as-is, no cross-document compose) is unaffected and remains
             what's shipped"}
   :consequence "the part-swap UI built this cycle was NOT shipped (reverted, no PR)
                rather than ship a visibly broken character -- this ADR's own
                fail-loudly invariant applied to itself"}
  :addendum_2607071730
  {:bug_2_fixed
   {:what "kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#2 (pin advanced): joint-set computation moved
           before mesh merge so it can build joint-index-of and rewrite every
           skinned mesh's JOINTS_0 data with real remapped values"
    :tolerance "a JOINTS_0 slot referencing an unmappable joint no longer throws
               unconditionally -- only when its paired WEIGHTS_0 is genuinely
               non-zero; real content commonly leaves harmless arbitrary indices
               in zero-weight slots from a whole-file shared skin"
    :verification "two new regression tests with unambiguous right/wrong answers
                  (reversed joint order; unmappable+zero-weight vs.
                  unmappable+real-weight), both confirmed to distinguish pre-fix
                  from post-fix behavior, not just non-crash. 44 tests/158
                  assertions"}
   :bug_3_open
   {:what "composing the ACTUAL real-world pair (Seed-san base + VRM1_
           Constraint_Twist_Sample donor hair) still throws, now on a DIFFERENT
           unmappable joint -- a full non-zero weight on a node whose name
           resolves to a leg-related bone, implausible for a hair vertex"
    :diagnosis_status "inconclusive this cycle -- an ad-hoc browser probe script
                       (hand-rolled cljs.core interop) produced CONTRADICTORY
                       results across two attempts about which of the donor's 3
                       skins the hair mesh's node actually references, meaning
                       the PROBE ITSELF is suspect, not necessarily compose"
    :next_step "add direct in-code diagnostics (a deftest against the actual
               Seed-san/VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample bytes) rather than more
               hand-rolled browser-script JS interop, so the diagnosis tool is
               held to the same rigor as the fixes"
    :blocks "net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI remains unshipped"}}
  :addendum_2607071800
  {:method "a direct clojure -M -e script against the actual downloaded .vrm bytes
            (vrm.parse/vrm.part/vrm.compose called directly, JVM ex-data inspected) --
            addendum 2's own recommendation, followed this time. Immediately caught
            that addendum 2's browser probe had read the WRONG skin (donor has 3
            skins; hair mesh uses skin 2; probe inspected skin 0) and reported a
            bogus node/bone name as a result"
   :bug_4_fixed
   {:what "the real unmappable-joint case carries weight 0.00266 (~0.27%), an
           ordinary blend-smoothing residual -- addendum 2's 1e-4 tolerance was too
           strict for real content"
    :fix "kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#3 (pin advanced): raised to 1e-2 (1%), with a test
         locking in the exact real-world value"}
   :bug_5_confirmed_bigger
   {:what "Seed-san has 5 SEPARATE skins, one per mesh (hair=23 joints,
           hair_tail=7, head=1, robo_arm=21, wear=80) -- compose's whole design
           assumes ONE shared skin per document (base-skin = first skin). A mesh
           using any other skin has joints joint-index-of doesn't contain, so even
           Seed-san's OWN wear/body mesh fails the unmappable-joint check against
           its OWN base document -- not a donor issue at all"
    :confidence "CONFIRMED with certainty this time (not addendum 2's
                'inconclusive') -- verified via the reliable direct-JVM method"
    :real_fix_scope "unify a document's own multiple skins into one before donor
                     merging, or extend composed output to support multiple skins --
                     a genuine architecture decision (likely its own ADR), not a
                     bounded patch"
    :blocks "net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI remains unshipped"}
   :lesson "the previous cycle's unreliable browser-script diagnosis was itself the
           obstacle -- switching to direct in-JVM calls against real bytes (no
           browser, no JS interop) resolved the ambiguity immediately and is the
           right default tool for future org-vrmc-vrm diagnosis"}
  :addendum_2607080100
  {:context "addendum 3 deferred the multi-skin question as 'a real architecture
             decision, not a bounded patch' -- revisited with a concrete design and
             found smaller than expected: the JOINTS_0 remap machinery (bug_2_fixed)
             was ALREADY skin-index-agnostic, only joint-set/IBM seeding assumed one
             skin per document"
   :bug_5_fixed
   {:what "kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#4 (pin advanced): joint-set seeding now unions
           EVERY skin any source document (base or donor) actually has, not just
           (first (:skins doc)); ibm-plan entries gained :skin-idx so the
           inverseBindMatrices build reads each joint's real matrix from whichever
           specific skin -- any document, any index -- it actually came from"
    :verification "new regression test mirrors the exact real failure shape (a
                   document's SOLE selected mesh using skin index 1, not 0) --
                   confirmed to fail pre-fix with the identical error signature as
                   the real Seed-san bug, pass with the fix. 46 tests/164 assertions.
                   Verified against the real Seed-san file (direct JVM diagnostic):
                   composing it as a base no longer fails on its own structure AT
                   ALL -- every one of its 5 skins now handled correctly"}
   :bug_6_open_narrower
   {:what "composing the full real pair (Seed-san + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample)
           still throws, but now on ONE different, precisely identified issue
           entirely on the donor side: J_Sec_Hair1_01, a genuine hair-sway
           secondary/physics bone with a real 4.1% skinning weight, parented under
           J_Bip_C_Head rather than under the hair mesh's own node"
    :root_cause "invisible to vrm.part/decompose's current node-indices heuristic
                (walks only the selected mesh's own node subtree) -- a vrm.part
                question, not a vrm.compose defect"
    :real_question "should a decomposed part's node-indices also include secondary/
                    spring-bone descendants of humanoid-bone ancestors, even when
                    they're not descendants of the mesh's own node? -- narrower and
                    more concrete than the open-ended 'architecture decision' this
                    addendum chain started with"
    :blocks "net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI remains unshipped, but the
             blocker is now singular and well-understood, not an open architecture
             question"}}
  :addendum_2607080800
  {:context "addendum 4 narrowed the remaining blocker to one precise question:
             should a decomposed part's node-indices also include secondary/
             spring-bone descendants of humanoid-bone ancestors, even when they're
             not descendants of the mesh's own node? -- answered yes, fixed in
             vrm.part (decompose defines what a part touches), not vrm.compose"
   :bug_7_fixed
   {:what "kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#5 (pin advanced): decompose now seeds a part's
           node-indices with every node the part's own mesh's JOINTS_0 vertex data
           genuinely resolves to (decoded the same way
           vrm.compose/remap-joints-accessor! does), on top of the existing pure
           descendant-walk"
    :self_caught_bug "an earlier draft seeded a whole skin's DECLARED :joints
                      palette unconditionally (not just the joints a mesh's own
                      vertices actually reference) -- wrong, since a skin is a
                      shared glTF object; this over-grew the unified skeleton with
                      joints no vertex in that mesh ever binds to. Caught via 5
                      real test regressions, diagnosed to the exact mechanism,
                      corrected to decode actual per-vertex JOINTS_0 values instead"
    :test_premise_updated "compose-still-throws-on-genuinely-weighted-unmappable-
                           joint's old fixture (a joint reachable via neither
                           humanoid-mapping nor node-indices) is now legitimately
                           resolved by this fix -- correctly so. Redesigned around
                           what remains a genuine defect: an out-of-range JOINTS_0
                           local-pos with no entry in the skin's own :joints array
                           at all (malformed data, not reachability)"
    :verification "new regression test (decompose-seeds-secondary-bone-not-a-
                   structural-descendant) reproduces the exact real-world topology
                   (secondary bone under Head, sibling to the mesh's own node, ~4%
                   weight matching J_Sec_Hair1_01's real ~4.1%) and is confirmed to
                   fail pre-fix with the identical error signature as the real bug
                   (ExceptionInfo ... no place in the unified skeleton, weight
                   0.04). Full suite: 47 tests/169 assertions, 0 failures"}
   :real_world_result
   {:what "composing the FULL real Seed-san (base, all 4 of its own decomposed
           parts) + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample's real hair as donor now succeeds
           end to end -- compose, GLB export, and reparse all complete without
           error (1 unified skin, 363 joints, 6 meshes, 424 nodes)"
    :method "re-downloaded both real files fresh from vrm-c/vrm-specification,
             direct JVM diagnostic (same established method as addenda 3-4)"
    :significance "the exact real-world avatar pair this addendum chain set out to
                   support composes cleanly for the first time -- the compose/
                   decompose engine investigation this ADR has tracked across 5
                   addenda is now closed"}
   :unblocks "net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI can be revisited on the
              strength of an engine proven against real, unmodified Consortium
              content, not synthetic fixtures alone"}}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "store exported .vrm blobs as the artifact of record"
   :rejected_because "opaque, undiffable, storage-heavy, hostile to kotobase-datomic; the
                      rebuild is deterministic so the blob is cache, not truth"}
  {:option "full mesh-modeling editor (VRoid Studio class)"
   :rejected_because "the engine does decompose/compose/recolor, not sculpting --
                      claiming otherwise is vaporware; dress-up composition is what the
                      engine supports and babiniku needs"}
  {:option "build the editor inside net-babiniku"
   :rejected_because "explicit user direction (kotoba-lang として); private vendor repo is
                      the wrong home for a reusable public lib; network-isekai is an
                      obvious second consumer"}
  {:option "name it vrm-editor"
   :rejected_because "editor is already the generic EDN-editor lib; Japanese product-name
                      family (murakumo/giemon/kenchi/itonami) is the org convention"}
  {:option "wire kotobase persistence now"
   :rejected_because "tested pure mapping makes the follow-up mechanical; blocking a pure
                      scaffold on live service wiring couples the wrong things"}]}